Read, edit, initialize and validate `instrukt.yaml`

Usage: instrukt config <COMMAND>

Commands:
  get       Print the value at a dotted path, or the whole configuration, interpolated. Reads the
            effective configuration (the global layer with the project layer applied) unless
            --global. With --agents, reads the effective agent selection literally
  show      Inspect machine-local configuration
  schema    Show what the addressed document can declare, from the types validation reads
  patch     Apply a merge patch (YAML mapping) to the project layer, the global layer with --global,
            or the agents file with --agents, if it is still at --revision
  init      Create the layer with the current schema version and defaults, or migrate an older
            project layer. Older machine layers require instrukt install. With --company, also
            append each ignore line the home's .gitignore lacks — /company.yaml, /secrets.env,
            /projects/ and /.instrukt/ — keeping every other line, in a new home or an existing one
  validate  Report the layer's findings; exits non-zero when there are any. With --company, two
            kinds: the configuration's, among them each local-only path the home's repository tracks
            or does not ignore, and the findings of rendering the home's AGENTS.md from its working
            tree
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
